@startuml qa-vs-qm
!pragma layout smetana
!theme plain
title Quality Assurance vs Quality Management in IG Development

skinparam rectangle {
  FontSize 11
  BorderColor #888888
}

rectangle "**Quality Management (QM)**\n— the navigation system —" as QM #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "Define maturity criteria\n(FMM 0–5)" as QM1 #DDEEFF
  rectangle "Govern stage transitions\n(WG · FMG · TSC)" as QM2 #DDEEFF
  rectangle "Establish ballot and\npublication processes" as QM3 #DDEEFF
  rectangle "Maintain backward-\ncompatibility policy" as QM4 #DDEEFF
}

rectangle "**Quality Assurance (QA)**\n— the navigation device in use —" as QA #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "CI-based interoperability\nmatrix testing (automated)" as QA1 #DDFBE8
  rectangle "Connectathon evidence\n(≥ 3 independent systems)" as QA2 #DDFBE8
  rectangle "FHIR validator checks\n(every build)" as QA3 #DDFBE8
  rectangle "Published test results\nby IG version" as QA4 #DDFBE8
}

QM -[hidden]right-> QA

note bottom of QA
  CI matrix testing lives here.
  It eliminates issues findable
  by automation — before they
  reach formal compliance gates.
end note

note bottom of QM
  Formal compliance testing
  and normative balloting
  live here.
end note

@enduml
